{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7691","id":5211443768,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNqBSOA","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7691","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7691.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7691.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7691","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7691/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7691/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7691/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/44a1bb023be03baa36aa0368e8d0f544a7b82830","number":7691,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs(id): reserved admin authority — LambdaMOO governance arc design note (#6004)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this adds\n\nThe design note for **#6004** (wave-2 follow-up of the worlds programme #5955, parent topic #5973): what authority id should reserve to the server/world admin **from day one**, and what is genuinely delegable to a world community — argued from LambdaMOO's documented 1990–1996 governance arc (wizards → 1992 devolution → 1993 ballot system → Mr. Bungle → 1996 recentralization).\n\nNew record: `doc/2026-11-08T12-50-00Z_design_id6004_lambdamoo_governance_arc/`, linked from `doc/README.md`.\n\n## Contents\n\n- **§1 Reserved authority** — a table of what cannot be outvoted, each row tied to the surface that already exists in `pkgs/id` (BUILDER install path, capability ceilings, admin token, resource envelope, MODERATOR revoke, host serving policy), with the two invariants that follow: no governance body may widen its own authority, and every exercise of reserved authority is a logged entry referencing what it changed.\n- **§2 Delegable to the community** — content rules and parameters, reviewer sets, appeals, pre-approval of in-world submissions, moderation-pack adoption/parameterization, and quota policy within the envelope. Includes the Mr. Bungle lesson mapped to id's actual surface: attribution is reserved (per-user function mapping #5967), delegation is always a strict subset (DELEGATE/attenuation), presentation may change how a participant looks but never who they are or what they did, and a moderation library never acts *as* a participant.\n- **§3 Quota as a governance tool** — LambdaMOO's base allocation plus discretionarily granted increases judged on quality/utility, read as the missing per-principal building quota in id; grants are logged content decisions, never envelope changes, and never a punishment lever.\n- **§4 The reserved-authority checklist** — 18 numbered items in three groups (world admin / host operator / delegable) plus the three platform invariants nobody delegates.\n\n## Scope\n\nDocs only, no code. The note supplies the authority split #5973's own deliverable must respect; it does not design the moderation-library interface, the pre-approval binding, or the quota data model (each named as a remaining decision in §5).\n\nCloses #6004.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796734147&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7691&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7691&signature=5edf55d383bd2a267c675bdb742170af43cab5f7e1d2017e019245b2588fdbd3\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7691?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added a design note outlining governance decisions, audit and appeal expectations, and quota recommendations, with historical context and related open questions.\n  * Added the note to the dated design-records index with a brief description and issue reference.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[{"id":12834280164,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAAC_PuS5A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/status/parked","name":"status/p